<section aria-labelledby="anytime-engagement-title">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="section-label">The campaign brief</div>
    <h2 id="anytime-engagement-title">Give former members a reason to come back.</h2>
    <p class="cs2-intro">The campaign reached people in Canada who had previously held an Anytime Fitness membership. They already knew the gym. We could start the conversation with the decision that mattered to them. Would they be interested in coming back if there was an incentive to reactivate their membership? <a href="https://www.anytimefitness.com/en-ca/membership">Explore Anytime Fitness memberships in Canada <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="anytime-campaign-title">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="section-label">How the calls worked</div>
    <h2 id="anytime-campaign-title">The incentive made the purpose of the call clear.</h2>
    <p class="cs2-intro">We contacted former members directly and explained what was available if they returned. The offer was tied to reactivating a membership, so the call could move from checking interest to asking for a sign-up.</p>
    <div class="cs2-signal-grid">
      <article><span>The opening</span><h3>Start from the previous membership</h3><p>The caller could refer to a relationship the member already had with the gym. The return offer gave them a specific reason to take another look at that membership.</p></article>
      <article><span>The outcome</span><h3>Measure completed sign-ups</h3><p>We tracked the result over six months. The figure counts former members who signed up again through the campaign.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
